{
  "_": [
    "What the simulated network answers, and for which URL. Bodies are real",
    "captures: tools/apicheck/check.py --save refreshes them from the live",
    "sources, so a fixture that drifts from the API gets caught by the same",
    "run that updates it.",
    "",
    "A match is the URL with the scheme stripped, compared without regard to",
    "case, and * stands for any run of characters. First match wins, so put the",
    "specific route above the general one.",
    "",
    "A URL nothing matches fails the fetch with 'no fixture', which is the",
    "honest answer: the view then draws its own error state, and a demo never",
    "shows one token's numbers under another token's name. That is why every",
    "token here is routed by its own address rather than by one wildcard.",
    "",
    "tools/fixtures/bundle.py compiles this into sim/src/fixtures.h."
  ],
